{"id":"meshullam","name":"Meshullam","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:meshullam"],"types":[{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Meshullam","text":"Befriended. (1.) One of the chief Gadites in Bashan in the time of Jotham (1 Chr. 5:13). (2.) Grandfather of Shaphan, “the scribe,” in the reign of Josiah (2 Kings 22:3). (3.) A priest, father of Hilkiah (1 Chr. 9:11; Neh. 11:11), in the reign of Ammon; called Shallum in 1 Chr. 6:12. (4.) A Levite of the family of Kohath (2 Chr. 34:12), in the reign of Josiah. (5.) 1 Chr. 8:17. (6.) 1 Chr. 3:19. (7.) Neh. 12:13. (8.) A chief priest (Neh. 12:16). (9.) One of the leading Levites in the time of Ezra (8:16). (10.) A priest (1 Chr. 9:12). (11.) One of the principal Israelites who supported Ezra when expounding the law to the people (Neh. 8:4)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4918","lemma":"מְשֻׁלָּם","xlit":"Mᵉshullâm","gloss":"Meshullam, the name of seventeen Israelites","kjv":"Meshullam","count":24,"share":1},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":14,"share":0.58},{"strong":"H2388","lemma":"חָזַק","xlit":"châzaq","gloss":"to fasten upon","kjv":"aid, amend, calker, catch","count":3,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","xlit":"ʻâmad","gloss":"to stand, in various relations","kjv":"abide, appoint, arise, cease","count":3,"share":0.13}],"verses":["2Kgs.22.3","1Chr.3.19","1Chr.5.13","1Chr.8.17","1Chr.9.7","1Chr.9.8","1Chr.9.11","1Chr.9.12","2Chr.34.12","Ezra.8.16","Ezra.10.15","Ezra.10.29","Neh.3.4","Neh.3.6","Neh.3.30","Neh.8.4","Neh.10.7","Neh.10.20","Neh.11.7","Neh.11.11","Neh.12.13","Neh.12.16","Neh.12.25","Neh.12.33"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"pe